### =========================================================================
### IsoTreatment - requests for the Strangler Fig migration stack
###
### Stack:  docker compose up -d --build
###   @gateway  :8080   YARP - the address the frontend uses
###   @monolith :8081   the monolith directly, for A/B comparison
###   Jaeger UI http://localhost:16686
###
### The API reads the JWT from an HttpOnly cookie named "token",
### never from an Authorization header.
###
### To mint a token without going through registration (user id 1),
### run from the repository root:
###
###   set -a; . ./.env; set +a
###   b64u() { openssl base64 -A | tr '+/' '-_' | tr -d '='; }
###   H=$(printf '%s' '{"alg":"HS256","typ":"JWT"}' | b64u)
###   P=$(printf '{"http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/ws/2005/05/identity/claims/nameidentifier":"1","exp":%s,"iss":"isotreatment-users-issuer","aud":"isotreatment-users-audience"}' $(( $(date +%s) + 3600 )) | b64u)
###   S=$(printf '%s' "$H.$P" | openssl dgst -sha256 -hmac "$AUTHENTICATION_SIGNING_KEY" -binary | b64u)
###   echo "$H.$P.$S"
### =========================================================================

@gateway = http://localhost:8080
@monolith = http://localhost:8081
@token = PASTE_TOKEN_HERE


### =========================================================================
### 1. Smoke tests - no authentication required
### =========================================================================

### Swagger is up  ->  200
GET {{gateway}}/swagger/index.html

### No cookie  ->  401, proves routing and authentication are wired
GET {{gateway}}/api/reminder

### Unknown path  ->  404
GET {{gateway}}/nie-ma-takiej-sciezki

### Unknown credentials  ->  400 "Invalid username or password"
### A 500 here means the database is unreachable or migrations never ran.
POST {{gateway}}/api/user/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "brak@example.com",
  "password": "brak"
}


### =========================================================================
### 2. User lifecycle
###
### Registration sends a confirmation e-mail and leaves EmailConfirmed = false,
### so login fails until the account is confirmed. For local work it is easier
### to seed a user with SQL and mint a token (see the header of this file).
### =========================================================================

### Register
POST {{gateway}}/api/user/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Jan",
  "lastName": "Kowalski",
  "email": "jan.kowalski@example.com",
  "password": "Haslo123!",
  "confirmPassword": "Haslo123!",
  "weight": 70,
  "climaxDoseInMiligramsPerKilogramOfBodyWeight": 120,
  "dailyDose": 40,
  "medicationStartDate": "2024-01-01T00:00:00"
}

### Confirm the e-mail (token arrives by e-mail)
POST {{gateway}}/api/user/confirmEmail?emailConfirmationToken=PASTE_CONFIRMATION_TOKEN

### Log in - the JWT comes back in a Set-Cookie header, not in the body
# @name login
POST {{gateway}}/api/user/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jan.kowalski@example.com",
  "password": "Haslo123!"
}

### Current user  ->  200
GET {{gateway}}/api/user/info
Cookie: token={{token}}

### Update the current user  ->  200
POST {{gateway}}/api/user/info/update
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: token={{token}}

{
  "firstName": "Jan",
  "lastName": "Nowak",
  "email": "jan.kowalski@example.com",
  "weight": 72,
  "climaxDoseInMiligramsPerKilogramOfBodyWeight": 120,
  "dailyDose": 40
}

### Log out - clears the cookie
POST {{gateway}}/api/user/logout
Cookie: token={{token}}


### =========================================================================
### 3. Reminders through the gateway
###
### This is the slice being extracted into the Treatment service.
### Note: POST returns 200 with no Location header, not 201.
### Time serializes as "08:00" (pl-PL culture), not "08:00:00".
### =========================================================================

### List  ->  200
GET {{gateway}}/api/reminder
Cookie: token={{token}}

### Create  ->  200 {"id":N,"time":"08:00"}
POST {{gateway}}/api/reminder
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: token={{token}}

{
  "time": "08:00"
}

### Read one  ->  200
GET {{gateway}}/api/reminder/1
Cookie: token={{token}}

### Update  ->  200
PUT {{gateway}}/api/reminder/1
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: token={{token}}

{
  "time": "21:15"
}

### Delete  ->  204 with an empty body
DELETE {{gateway}}/api/reminder/1
Cookie: token={{token}}

### Missing reminder  ->  404 "Reminder not found", plain text, no Content-Type
GET {{gateway}}/api/reminder/999999
Cookie: token={{token}}


### =========================================================================
### 4. The same reminders, straight to the monolith
###
### Run these next to the ones above: the gateway is transparent only if the
### status, the body and the headers match. This pair becomes the contract
### test in Phase 5, with the Treatment service on one side.
### =========================================================================

### List  ->  must be identical to the gateway response
GET {{monolith}}/api/reminder
Cookie: token={{token}}

### Create
POST {{monolith}}/api/reminder
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: token={{token}}

{
  "time": "20:30"
}

### Missing reminder  ->  404
GET {{monolith}}/api/reminder/999999
Cookie: token={{token}}


### =========================================================================
### 5. Diary entries
### =========================================================================

### List  ->  200
GET {{gateway}}/api/entry
Cookie: token={{token}}

### Create  ->  200
POST {{gateway}}/api/entry
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: token={{token}}

{
  "content": "Skin looks better, no side effects today.",
  "date": "2026-08-28T00:00:00"
}

### Update  ->  200
PUT {{gateway}}/api/entry/1
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: token={{token}}

{
  "content": "Corrected note."
}

### Delete  ->  204
DELETE {{gateway}}/api/entry/1
Cookie: token={{token}}


### =========================================================================
### 6. Treatment process calculation
### =========================================================================

### Stateless calculation from the user's pharmacological parameters  ->  200
GET {{gateway}}/api/treatment-process
Cookie: token={{token}}


### =========================================================================
### 7. CORS preflight
###
### Both ports must answer identically, with exactly ONE
### Access-Control-Allow-Origin header. Two of them means CORS was added to
### the gateway as well - which breaks browsers while leaving curl happy.
### =========================================================================

### Preflight through the gateway  ->  204
OPTIONS {{gateway}}/api/reminder
Origin: http://localhost:5173
Access-Control-Request-Method: GET

### Preflight straight to the monolith  ->  204, same headers
OPTIONS {{monolith}}/api/reminder
Origin: http://localhost:5173
Access-Control-Request-Method: GET


### =========================================================================
### 8. Authentication edge cases
### =========================================================================

### Token in the Authorization header instead of the cookie  ->  401
### The monolith only ever reads the cookie. The Treatment service will have
### to accept both, because the Branch by Abstraction path uses the header.
GET {{gateway}}/api/reminder
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Malformed token  ->  401
GET {{gateway}}/api/reminder
Cookie: token=not.a.jwt


### =========================================================================
### 9. Generating traffic for Jaeger
###
### Fire these, then open http://localhost:16686 and look for ONE trace
### spanning gateway -> monolith -> SQL. Two unlinked traces mean the
### traceparent header is not being propagated across the proxy.
### =========================================================================

### Through the gateway - should produce a two-service trace
GET {{gateway}}/api/reminder
Cookie: token={{token}}

### Straight to the monolith - should produce a single-service trace
GET {{monolith}}/api/reminder
Cookie: token={{token}}
